[TITLE] kubectl cannot process listed objects in json file [BODY] kubectl cannot process the following listed objects (copied from
here
)
[{
  "apiVersion": "v1beta2",
  "kind": "Secret",
  "id": "prod-db-secret",
  "data": {
    "username": "dmFsdWUtMQ0K",
    "password": "dmFsdWUtMg0KDQo="
  }
},
{
  "apiVersion": "v1beta2",
  "kind": "Secret",
  "id": "test-db-secret",
  "data": {
    "username": "dmFsdWUtMQ0K",
    "password": "dmFsdWUtMg0KDQo="
  }
}]
$ kubectl create -f ...
Error: unable to get type info from "double.json": couldn't get version/kind: json: cannot unmarshal array into Go value of type struct { APIVersion string "json:\"apiVersion,omitempty\""; Kind string "json:\"kind,omitempty\"" }
#7257
states "Group related objects together in a single file. This currently requires a List object in YAML, but it's still better than separate files. Almost nobody knows about this feature." Does this feature only work for YAML but not JSON? Thanks.
@bgrant0607
@krousey
@nikhiljindal

