[TITLE] Publish kubernetes protocol definitions as .proto files [BODY] This is probably not a right place to request this, but I didn't find anything on discuss.kubernetes.io or Google.
I have a number of services around kubernetes cluster, that would greatly benefit from original protocol definitions used by kubernetes itself. For example I could have a gRPC handler returning deployments/services/pods currently running in my cluster with some additional metainfo outside of kubernetes:
message Response {
    my_namespace.DeploymentMeta meta = 1;
    k8s.apps.v1.Deployment deployment = 2;
}

service MyAwesomeService {
    rpc ListDeployments (google.protobuf.Empty) returns (stream Response);
}
To achieve this I would need original
.proto
files for stuff I'm interested in (e.g.
Deployment
,
Service
,
Pod
,
DaemonSet
, etc.), but I didn't find it anywhere (I think I read somewhere that protobuf definitions are actually generated from Go-structs).
Also it would be great to have functions for conversion from Go-struct and protobuf message and back.
Is is possible to provide these things?

