[TITLE] The GCE cloudprovider's functions and assumptions should be documented [BODY] Is this a BUG REPORT or FEATURE REQUEST?
(choose one):
DOCS REQUEST
@bowei
I'm trying out the cloud-controller-manager on top of kubeadm in line with proposal
https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/design-proposals/cloud-provider-refactoring.md
But the assumptions the GCE cloudprovider makes are non-obvious, for example setting some tags somewhere on a node for being able to create LB Services.
I already had
@jlowdermilk
help me a little on Slack, but currently the whole cloudprovider stuff is kind of a black box and I'd want us to change that.
@jbeda
did a doc like this for AWS already and I'd like to make that a pattern across cloudproviders, document these in a centralized manner and eventually move these out of repo when we have everything cleared out.
@wlan0
,
@thockin
@roberthbailey
and myself are driving the cloudprovider refactoring.
@bowei
As mentioned on Slack, I'll assign the GCE parts of this issue to you.

[TITLE] StatefulSet Partitioned strategy vs parameterized Roll out strategy [BODY] Prior to 1.7 release we should decide on keeping the PartitionedStatefulSetStrategy documented in the design for StatefulSet update, or, instead, adding an optional ordinal parameter to the RollingUpdateStatefulSetStrategy. The deviation is described below.
// StatefulSetUpdateStrategy indicates the strategy that the StatefulSet
// controller will use to perform updates. It includes any additional parameters
// necessary to perform the update for the indicated strategy.
type
StatefulSetUpdateStrategy
struct
{
// Type indicates the type of the StatefulSetUpdateStrategy.
Type
StatefulSetUpdateStrategyType
`json:"type,omitempty" protobuf:"bytes,1,opt,name=type,casttype=StatefulSetStrategyType"`
// Partition is used to communicate the optional ordinal at which to partition
// the StatefulSet when Type is RollingUpdateStatefulSetStrategyType. This
// value may only be set when the Type is RollingUpdateStatefulSetStrategyType,
// and it must be nil otherwise.
Partition
*
RollingUpdatePartition
`json:"partition,omitempty" protobuf:"bytes,2,opt,name=partition"`
}
// RollingUpdatePartition is used to indicate a partition in the StatefulSet during a Rolling Update.
type
RollingUpdatePartition
struct
{
// Ordinal indicates the ordinal at which the StatefulSet should be
// partitioned. All Pods with an ordinal greater than or equal to partition will receive the update.
Ordinal
int32
`json:"ordinal" protobuf:"varint,1,opt,name=ordinal"`
}

